#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119526 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "4efedc4e-19e9-552c-bc27-814df953e141" :question/math-academy-id "e-4575" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "311ba12f-de22-580c-9e0d-6766f7864d1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4578" :question/problem "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+ky=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059292/assets/a404c14afc5aeda319edcad04d7ea6f7f9ee0631f3a86c567a48f448dc21de8e.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059292/assets/648ce0c1b8b77c1230c6c634c676624f9c79c12ffc3942abc09d24d0fdc424d3.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059292/assets/f23784cb494ee42a65b07597b9f287b107b81502fba3a51b22344d804ee937a8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\dfrac{D_y}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{36}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "d81e32a1-bd93-5a95-bb4a-e8df9063b5aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5230" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059292/assets/2d3571405367c6d4ce15927a1dbdb50a30af7d13580c7b9cd3c73bada0583c98.png)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b698822-324b-5a2a-b201-40054afc1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335077} {:answer/id #uuid "6899dc1a-2662-5d3e-a868-8805c0f3a4bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335078} {:answer/id #uuid "85e33954-33ed-5008-aec1-aa1f1259f3ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 17\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335079} {:answer/id #uuid "af0453aa-99b8-56ca-898c-ad63d492aa5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335080} {:answer/id #uuid "5640075d-cf38-587f-b6e7-b3f1bd03fd08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b698822-324b-5a2a-b201-40054afc1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e22a3cf1-0e45-55ec-bf4a-355272f9dd76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3dee3a3d-b589-52d5-8b29-2264540bb947" :question/math-academy-id "q-139960" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a6625a9-0cbb-5d69-831e-42ed9c34b8f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335097} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b03701-9bf7-5704-9400-efc75b897a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335098} {:answer/id #uuid "e4bbd7c9-8930-5ee8-bc6f-5f7a8c019383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335099} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6a0891-e60b-5a38-84db-bdc915719ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,3 & 15 \\\\ -2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335100} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2c8935-3dfc-5612-a3f6-4aecbcf5bbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb2c8935-3dfc-5612-a3f6-4aecbcf5bbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335101} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d53fa8d-1654-53d1-9a47-803744d17efb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c2e31ac-502a-53cd-a44d-a0ec535a4195" :question/math-academy-id "q-42606" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06094f01-ac5b-59bb-9c54-335bcb14a3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 15\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337706} {:answer/id #uuid "911dc0d8-2796-5277-b06d-c262cd790f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337707} {:answer/id #uuid "6db015ec-4b00-59fc-8b2a-6a1bbe3dbbf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 32 \\\\ -3 & 26\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337708} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb47040-ab75-5c0b-b667-b1043fdfec1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337709} {:answer/id #uuid "812331f5-ca06-53c4-89f0-29502fd4066e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "911dc0d8-2796-5277-b06d-c262cd790f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337707} :answer-field/id #uuid "07d4347c-41b6-538c-a4f8-23bffdefd889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dfded1e-a7d9-55f5-89b7-27037faf3f8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42607" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+6y=32 \\\\ 3x+5y=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+6y=32 \\\\ 3x+5y=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f2b7c4-9915-5240-8e71-f70a338c04b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337713} {:answer/id #uuid "57085387-1f04-578f-ac35-cfaec61bb54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :ans