mn of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e306af7-8a6f-5c3b-a6fc-59d6b6e1c77b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337720} {:answer/id #uuid "a4857ade-95aa-52c8-8e14-977edb3fa39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 14 \\\\ 6 & -10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337721} {:answer/id #uuid "42477dc3-6c56-5ecd-83b8-e860bd9e741b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}12 & 10 \\\\ -7 & -14\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337722} {:answer/id #uuid "a092f408-03d4-5e04-8cae-a790598e14d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337723} {:answer/id #uuid "125f2b53-c1b4-54e4-ae20-d9bccd123e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -14\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a092f408-03d4-5e04-8cae-a790598e14d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337723} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f18706-d852-58ef-b1cc-48ff9482de87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "601b7557-a1a8-5ebf-8aa6-23fd01fa3f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42610" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+12y=10 \\\\ 6x-7y=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+12y=10 \\\\ 6x-7y=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1cf87b-86ee-5a28-aee8-a94a783f4029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118672} {:answer/id #uuid "fe57ecbc-9dc4-5d6c-8c75-6926c3f0aef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118673} {:answer/id #uuid "1b78bc06-a44f-5553-aeb1-e3d92b3dc629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118674} {:answer/id #uuid "6461d045-0c05-5d7d-9d69-0f125ccba0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118675} {:answer/id #uuid "789901ab-878d-57bc-81f2-a2e41769d2aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe57ecbc-9dc4-5d6c-8c75-6926c3f0aef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118673} :answer-field/id #uuid "40d08632-e306-52e6-ab97-ed6dfef36ddc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "14b8a882-c4c9-5cd4-86d8-6c02afbea2c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42612" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-y=k \\\\ -2x+4y=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=-6$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=-54$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=18$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =20-2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|}{18} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}| & =-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271c346f-48e5-5989-931c-c9f3fb5caab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335111} {:answer/id #uuid "07927c49-daa6-599c-99a3-151ad9664a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335112} {:answer/id #uuid "58786e39-375f-5c88-bf3b-57b71a14ddb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335113} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5cbc82-821d-546d-9470-35ee16eaaa68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335114} {:answer/id #uuid "5e40c96e-c9bd-5724-8916-6682b2018ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58786e39-375f-5c88-bf3b-57b71a14ddb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335113} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c1d2ba-bbf2-5aca-8c0c-7c5e798319ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff9ce129-3900-5770-b561-66ce2c4a5268" :question/math-academy-id "q-42613" :question/problem "Let $⟨-4,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+11y=-14 \\\\ 6x-ky=-34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 1 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $-4|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82becbd4-494e-51ec-b394-8bedbea10379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,7 & 13 \\\\ -5 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335118} {:answer/id #uuid "11243639-943e-5bfb-a34c-de52a98d61fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335119} {:answer/id #uuid "c690e8e3-2d8b-51c3-a855-be53aebb7423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,13 & 7 \\\\ 19 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335120} {:answer/id #uuid "a77f0a77-582f-5eb8-ad33-74421fbbbd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & 13 \\\\ -4 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335121} {:answer/id #uuid "e2bd768d-2c7d-51c6-8b03-5b63b5110a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}13 & \\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ 19 & -2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11243639-943e-5bfb-a34c-de52a98d61fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335119} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa457e1d-9b2b-5b7c-9211-e5239cbd3fd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69a6ad9d-656e-51bb-9c61-6471ddfbd822" :question/math-academy-id "q-42970" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe7f24e8-0cf2-505c-bc02-379e24a173e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 175921