t column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1bbd18d-4159-593a-8ac9-4e184c255ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337733} {:answer/id #uuid "30714c61-e3de-5fa5-8256-a9598c7b79af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-6 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337734} {:answer/id #uuid "e53d1a04-076c-5a48-b4a3-02392a9aae17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & \\,\\,-6\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337735} {:answer/id #uuid "6359e2f8-3431-5da3-a90d-e3cb4ffc3bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\,\\,-6 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337736} {:answer/id #uuid "80763d73-02cf-5411-a8a5-a1c03d652c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-6 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80763d73-02cf-5411-a8a5-a1c03d652c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-6 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337737} :answer-field/id #uuid "4226d979-1f16-5993-94af-c7ee6f586a35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11088c08-8da3-5080-8dbb-7306ba9755d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42979" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-6 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,x+y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-6 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,x+y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-6 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db4c549a-520d-5bec-ab5b-0cde986a55e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337740} {:answer/id #uuid "49349261-72ae-578a-9fed-d2b0ad8464b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337741} {:answer/id #uuid "51af9672-5581-53c7-87e0-9cc6c3346f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337742} {:answer/id #uuid "faa1a6ab-a8a3-5cf4-b804-f7a54df193c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337743} {:answer/id #uuid "c706bdd6-e086-5e4e-9b5c-093007ca1468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51af9672-5581-53c7-87e0-9cc6c3346f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cea0d5a-09a5-54a4-9b3c-c55cc44107a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "953305f0-133b-50fe-9ae2-f34d2c4d063f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42984" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=k \\\\ 2x-y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-13$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=13$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3-10 \\\\  & -13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|}{-13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)(-13) \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d42042-434d-5a69-aacc-193880c3c2d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335152} {:answer/id #uuid "5506e7ea-4684-502f-a34b-5360e1da77aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335153} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7440b8-7c4a-5380-8837-6cd2205c7b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335155} {:answer/id #uuid "126916aa-c8be-5d9d-822a-919524a2ad50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8c6a4e-1f22-5f7e-b077-0f7db42cd782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d47b44f-bbb3-54e7-8ca3-2db255852117" :question/math-academy-id "q-70201" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\,\\,1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd05303-f84e-5c67-b25f-01fc8466c943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335159} {:answer/id #uuid "744e467e-bda6-53b3-b523-5d32ebad0211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335160} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} {:answer/id #uuid "3791b02d-ebb5-586f-a80d-c9c0f6c0d972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335162} {:answer/id #uuid "4330df1e-c834-580d-9cec-35670e81873f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} :answer-field/id #uuid "37292bee-6ead-58b3-9354-c6080811ad1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "745a2d2f-9203-593c-9a03-87c0afb1d76b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70252" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6804615-a03f-5769-89d6-0139222dac77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337747} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1b4cca-6a1c-52b9-a70a-092c79f76feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337748} {:answer/id #uuid "d66fcc06-0477-5fa1-b879-13e3adf7640a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337749} {:answer/id #uuid "5382a98c-bffb-5d5f-832c-c7819b38eafe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337750} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc4c6fa-c7c1-579d-b242-0136f36a56a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d66fcc06-0477-5fa1-b879-13e3adf7640a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337749} :answer-field/id #uuid "259ff49f-f819-556d-8fce-1ebefe1e16d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94153e84-a333-5aec-b75c-49c1a118f48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77398" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45a679bd-d562-5041-aabe-d65749d03bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337754} {:answer/id #uuid "7203f23b-8a1a-565d-8148-3c42049259b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337755} {:answer/id #uuid "6a849391-049e-5155-927a-b2988a5b6646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337756} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd1748-b376-5df1-8db0-b1ae41e5df24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337757} {:answer/id #uuid "42681e5b-6888-52c8-9ed4-7dbbebbafab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a849391-049e-5155-927a-b2988a5b6646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337756} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e53c100-1fca-5ca9-9f15-0b515cdfbd84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "756e58e6-b552-5d33-821c-20311fcd965f" :question/math-academy-id "q-77400" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-6$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=3$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|}{3} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}]}
